This product includes software and design ideas re-implemented from the
following open-source projects. Where code was ported, it was re-implemented
in Rust; no upstream source files are vendored. Attribution is provided here
in good faith and to satisfy upstream license terms.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
code-review-graph — https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 Tirth Kanani)
  Used by: illuminate-index (the recursive-CTE impact/flow traversal shape) and
  illuminate-audit (the risk-scoring model and band ladder). The upstream is
  Python; the risk model and traversal were re-implemented in Rust.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
reflect — https://github.com/rohansx/reflect
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 Rohan)
  Used by: illuminate-eval (the deterministic, offline parse-and-score verdict
  model — EvalSignal/Severity, stdout parsers, Laplace confidence scoring, and
  the near-duplicate lesson gate). The LLM-judge portions of reflect are NOT
  ported; illuminate-eval is deterministic and never calls a model.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
codebase-memory-mcp — https://github.com/DeusData/codebase-memory-mcp
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2025 DeusData)
  Used by: illuminate-layout (the 3D force-directed layout, a Rust port of
  layout3d.c) and the /graph react-three-fiber renderer technique.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
homn — https://github.com/rohansx/homn
  License: Apache-2.0 (homn-policy)
  Used by: illuminate-policy (the Rhai deny→ask→allow policy engine), ported
  from homn-policy and relicensed MIT with the author's permission.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
headroom — https://github.com/chopratejas/headroom
  License: Apache-2.0 (Copyright 2025 Headroom Contributors)
  Used by: illuminate-compress (the SmartCrusher statistical JSON-compaction
  heuristics — gate, head/tail anchors, error/anomaly/rare-status/structural
  keep-sets, dedup, and the dropped-rows marker). Re-implemented in Rust from
  the algorithm; no upstream source is vendored. The CCR cache/retrieve layer
  is NOT ported — illuminate-compress is the lossy compressor only.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GitNexus
  Not vendored or derived. illuminate-query re-implements a bounded
  openCypher-subset query surface from the public openCypher grammar and from
  GitNexus's observable MCP tool surface only; no GitNexus source is used.
